#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096368 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in One Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "0a5391bf-06ef-5099-a835-0375ff96c342" :question/math-academy-id "e-1038" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0.5x+3y+4 &=0 \\\\ 4x &=-20y-20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the first equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0.5x+3y+4 &=0 && |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 4x &=-20y-20 && \\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe also notice that each equation can be simplified by dividing by a common factor. In the first equation, the common factor is $5,$ while in the second equation, the common factor is $4.$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+30y+40 &=0 && |\\,÷5 \\\\ 4x &=-20y-20 && |\\,÷4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNotice that the second equation is already solved for $x.$ So, we can substitute $x = -5y-5$ into the first equation and then solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+6y+8 & =0 \\\\ (-5y-5)+6y+8 & =0 \\\\ y+3 & =0 \\\\ y & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $x,$ we substitute $y=-3$ back into $x=-5y-5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-5y-5 \\\\  & =-5(-3)-5 \\\\  & =15-5 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 10$ and $y = -3,$ which can be expressed as $(10, -3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096369 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096785 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in Both Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "8f4b321d-ebc7-5f78-9bde-b51b297a0cc0" :question/math-academy-id "e-1039" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1.4x+2.8y &=1.4 \\\\ 0.02x+0.01y &=0.05\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the first equation by $10$ and the second equation by $100,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1.4x+2.8y &=1.4 && |\\times 10 \\\\ 0.02x+0.01y &=0.05 && |\\times 100\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo simplify the first equation, we divide by $14\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}14x+28y &=14 && |÷14 \\\\ 2x+y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Notice that the first equation can easily be solved for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y & =1 \\\\ x & =1-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can substitute $x=1-2y$ into the second equation and then solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y & =5 \\\\ 2(1-2y)+y & =5 \\\\ 2-4y+y & =5 \\\\ 2-3y & =5 \\\\ -3y & =3 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $x,$ we substitute $y=-1$ back into $x=1-2y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =1-2y \\\\  & =1-2(-1) \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x =3$ and $y =-1$, which can be expressed as $(3, -1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in One Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e595558-a7b5-5d7e-a16f-ecdb52280ea7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535463} {:answer/id #uuid "227a8863-645d-5b6a-927f-2a72b437610f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "192" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535488} {:answer/id #uuid "568f958f-3170-5ebb-9dbd-ad93f7c5fe07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535572} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b59232-9050-5b0c-8245-2c74284bbb90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535686} {:answer/id #uuid "eb27dbfa-ca02-5d9c-abad-838dbe761243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "196" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "568f958f-3170-5ebb-9dbd-ad93f7c5fe07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535572} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c91a14a-bb0b-5009-a73f-c0026c98e31c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4ed7da6-2468-5aec-962f-cfbcbb62e8fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-18697" :question/problem "Let $(x,y)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $x-y?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0.04x-0.08y-4=0 \\\\ 2x-3y=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the top equation by $100,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0.04x-0.08y-4=0 & |\\,\\times 100 \\\\ 2x-3y=4 & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-8y-400=0 \\\\ 2x-3y=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $-2,$ we will get a $-4x$ term in the second equation that can cancel with the $4x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-8y-400=0 &  \\\\ 2x-3y=4 & |\\,\\times (-2)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-8y-400=0 \\\\ -4x+6y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{4x}-8y-400 & =0 \\\\ -\\cancel{4x}+6y & =-8 \\\\ (-8y+6y)-400 & =-8 \\\\ -2y & =392 \\\\ y & =-196\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $y=-196$ into the equation $2x-3y=4$ to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3y & =4 \\\\ 2x-3(-196) & =4 \\\\ 2x+588 & =4 \\\\ 2x & =-584 \\\\ x & =-292\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-292$ and $y=-196.$ So, \n\n$$\nx-y=-292-(-196)=-292+196=-96.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in One Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18379570-3573-56f1-ab2f-409230c665e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285002} {:answer/id #uuid "2048a0a2-d38b-500f-b1cf-d208a4910fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285079} {:answer/id #uuid "33624308-466d-5a86-b996-91ff0395f5fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285256} {:answer/id #uuid "49c9eb6f-216d-5f7c-b9c2-9868dccfc81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285469} {:answer/id #uuid "d6430e16-c3e1-5238-9e78-0f4ef31b5445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18379570-3573-56f1-ab2f-409230c665e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285002} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c3a2076-6fe5-5f27-acde-2eb1abd84aed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "156c3b0d-28fb-58f6-9d7c-fb391142fe01" :question/math-academy-id "q-18702" :question/problem "Let $(x,y)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $x-y?$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2.3x+4.6y &=69 \\\\ 10x-20y &=100\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the top equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2.3x+4.6y &=69 && |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 10x-20y &=100 && \\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}23x+46y &=690 \\\\ 10x-20y &=100\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNotice that if we divide the first equation by $23$ and the second equation by $10,$ we will get a $2y$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $-2y$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}23x+46y &=690 && |\\,÷23 \\\\ 10x-20y &=100 && |\\,÷10\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=30 \\\\ x-2y &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $y$-variable and allows us to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\cancel{2y} & =30 \\\\ x-\\cancel{2y} & =10 \\\\ (x+x) & =(30+10) \\\\ 2x & =40 \\\\ x & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $x=20$ into the equation $x+2y=30$ to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y & =30 \\\\ (20)+2y & =30 \\\\ 2y & =30-20 \\\\ 2y & =10 \\\\ y & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=20$ and $y=5.$ So, \n\n$$\nx-y=20-(5)=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096785 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in Both Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21d7b079-5b50-5b5d-a77e-c9a71268f693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=2.25,\\,q=0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535486} {:answer/id #uuid "4eb64a1d-8845-5aea-9803-8f15099d25a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=1.25,\\,q=-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535552} {:answer/id #uuid "4fbd9059-e12a-555b-8cce-f4bef805bb62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=4.75,\\,q=5.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535555} {:answer/id #uuid "65c25a18-a5c0-51c1-96fe-a97b57c8f7e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=6.5,\\,q=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535594} {:answer/id #uuid "77264515-b435-5964-ac00-91f1b1107f1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=3.5,\\,q=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21d7b079-5b50-5b5d-a77e-c9a71268f693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=2.25,\\,q=0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535486} :answer-field/id #uuid "92d9c867-3aea-504b-83f3-0aeca8e42f08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3cdb6891-b142-501a-b07a-0a0cfaa8a9db" :question/math-academy-id "q-18823" :question/problem "Find the solution of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0.2p+0.3q=0.6 \\\\ 0.2p-0.1q=0.4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0.2p+0.3q=0.6 & |\\times 10 \\\\ 0.2p-0.1q=0.4 & |\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}2p+3q=6 \\\\ 2p-q=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that if we multiply the second equation by $-1,$ then we will get a $-2p$ term that can cancel with the $2p$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2p+3q=6 &  \\\\ 2p-q=4 & |\\,\\times (-1)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}2p+3q=6 \\\\ -2p+q=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $p$-variable and allows us to solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{2p}+3q & =6 \\\\ -\\cancel{2p}+q & =-4 \\\\ (3q+q) & =(6-4) \\\\ 4q & =2 \\\\ q & =\\frac{2}{4} \\\\ q & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $q=0.5$ into the equation $2p-q=4$ to solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p-q & =4 \\\\ 2p-0.5 & =4 \\\\ 2p & =4.5 \\\\ p & =\\frac{4.5}{2} \\\\ p & =2.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=2.25,\\,q=0.5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096785 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in Both Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2728a05c-b733-5d7a-a3ee-efdd536081bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535496} {:answer/id #uuid "84d0281f-81cf-5464-888b-3fb42539c91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535646} {:answer/id #uuid "d216a963-8190-5dc8-93bb-49be306033dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535756} {:answer/id #uuid "f89943d7-a9b6-59a5-95a6-1c63bacee9df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535816} {:answer/id #uuid "ffe0850c-bd3b-535d-bfb0-aada34fa3333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84d0281f-81cf-5464-888b-3fb42539c91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535646} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e101cd2-0992-5de6-9b2d-4f35a8656511" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd60924f-af00-5e97-9e77-c29eb2bc8035" :question/math-academy-id "q-18855" :question/problem "Let $(x,y)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $x+y?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0.05x-0.03y=0.04 \\\\ 0.4x+0.2y=0.1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the first equations by $100$ and the second equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0.05x-0.03y=0.04 & |\\times 100 \\\\ 0.4x+0.2y=0.1 & |\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y=4 \\\\ 4x+2y=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$ and the second equation by $3,$ we will get a $-6y$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $6y$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y=4 & |\\,\\times (2) \\\\ 4x+2y=1 & |\\,\\times (3)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-6y=8 \\\\ 12x+6y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $y$-variable and allows us to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10x-\\cancel{6y} & =8 \\\\ 12x+\\cancel{6y} & =3 \\\\ (10x+12x) & =(8+3) \\\\ 22x & =11 \\\\ x & =\\frac{11}{22} \\\\ x & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $x=0.5$ into the equation $4x+2y=1$ to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2y & =1 \\\\ 4(0.5)+2y & =1 \\\\ 2+2y & =1 \\\\ 2y & =-1 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=0.5$ and $y=-0.5.$ So, \n\n$$\nx+y=0.5+(-0.5)=0.\n$$"}]}
